{"surah": 97, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِنَّآ أَنزَلْنَٰهُ فِى لَيْلَةِ ٱلْقَدْرِ ", "translation": "Indeed, We sent it [i.e., the Qur’ān] down during the Night of Decree.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّآ", "translit": "ٓāَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَنزَلْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْlَznَaʾ", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَيْلَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ ", "translation": "And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَدْرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَيْلَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ خَيْرٌ مِّنْ أَلْفِ شَهْرٍ ", "translation": "The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَيْلَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَlْyَl", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْقَدْرِ", "translit": "ِrْdَqْlٱ", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "خَيْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْyَhk", "root": "خير"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مِّنْ", "translit": "ْnِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَلْفِ", "translit": "ِfْlَaʾ", "root": "الف"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "شَهْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْhَhs", "root": "شهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "تَنَزَّلُ ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ وَٱلرُّوحُ فِيهَا بِإِذْنِ رَبِّهِم مِّن كُلِّ أَمْرٍ ", "translation": "The angels and the Spirit [i.e., Gabriel] descend therein by permission of their Lord for every matter.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "تَنَزَّلُ", "translit": "ُlَّzَnَt", "root": "نزل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَkِyʾَٰٓlَmْlٱ", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَٱلرُّوحُ", "translit": "ُḥwُّrlٱَw", "root": "روح"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِإِذْنِ", "translit": "ِnْhdِiʾِb", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّهِم", "translit": "mِhِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "مِّن", "translit": "nِّm", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "كُلِّ", "translit": "ِّlُk", "root": "كلل"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "أَمْرٍ", "translit": "ٍrْmَaʾ", "root": "امر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "سَلَٰمٌ هِىَ حَتَّىٰ مَطْلَعِ ٱلْفَجْرِ ", "translation": "Peace it is[1] until the emergence of dawn.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "سَلَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰlَs", "root": "سلم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هِىَ", "translit": "َàِh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حَتَّىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَّtَḥ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَطْلَعِ", "translit": "ِʿعَlْṭَm", "root": "طلع"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْفَجْرِ", "translit": "ِrْjgَfْlٱ", "root": "فجر"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"1": [{"arabic": "ركعة يفصل بين كل ركعتين بتسليمة يقرأ في كل ركعة بفاتحة الكتاب مرة وإنا أنزلناه في ليلة القدر ثلاث مرات وقل هو الله أحد اثنتي عشرة مرة فإذا فرغ من صلاته صلى علي سبعين مرة يقول اللهم صل على محمد النبي الأمي وعلى آله ثم يسجد ويقول في سجوده سبعين مرة سبوح قدوس رب الملائكة والروح ثم يرفع رأسه ويقول سبعين مرة رب اغفر وارحم وتجاوز عما تعلم إنك أنت الأعز الأكرم ثم يسجد سجدة أخرى ويقول فيها مثل ما قال في السجدة الأولى ثم يسأل حاجته في سجوده فإنها تقضى (4) قال رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم لا يصلي أحد هذه الصلاة إلا غفر الله تعالى له", "english": "**The First:** The takbīr (declaration of Allah's Greatness). Its beginning is established by the saying of Allah, the Exalted: {«وَتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللَّهَ عَلَى مَا هَدَاكُمْ»} (\"And that you complete the number and magnify Allah for having guided you\") {Al-Baqarah: 185}. Its form is that one says: \"Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar, lā ilāha illā Allāhu wa-Allāhu akbar, Allāhu akbar wa-li-Llāhi al-ḥamd\" (Allah is Greater, Allah is Greater, there is no deity except Allah, and Allah is Greater, Allah is Greater, and to Allah belongs all praise). And it is said: \"Allāhu akbar kabīran, wa-al-ḥamdu li-Llāhi kathīran, wa-subḥāna Allāhi bukratan wa-aṣīlā, lā ilāha illā Allāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lah, mukhlisīna lahu al-dīn wa-law kariha al-kāfirūn\" (Allah is Greater, abundantly great, and praise be to Allah, abundantly much, and glory be to Allah morning and evening. There is no deity except Allah alone, with no partner, sincere to Him in religion, even though the disbelievers detest it). One begins the takbīr on the night of Fiṭr until the commencement of the Eid prayer. In the second Eid (al-Aḍḥā), one begins the takbīr immediately after the dawn prayer on the Day of ʿArafah until the end of the day of the thirteenth [of Dhū al-Ḥijjah]. This is the most complete of the sayings. One pronounces the takbīr after the obligatory prayers and after the supererogatory prayers, though it is more emphatic after the obligatory ones.", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 162", "section_title_en": "The Book of the Revival of the Religious Sciences — Section on the Two Festivals (Eid), the Supererogatory Prayers of Rajab and Shaʿbān", "section_index": 162, "anchors": "- Root: كبر (k-b-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of greatness in magnitude, age, or rank; al-takbīr is the utterance \"Allāhu akbar\" (Allah is Greater).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-kabīr and al-ṣaghīr are relative terms; takbīr in worship signifies declaring Allah's transcendence above all comparison, used in quantity (connected/disconnected) and in dignity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"Allāhu akbar\" as magnification of Allah's majesty. Metaphorical (majāz): \"takabbara\" for prideful self-aggrandizement (blameworthy), distinct from the liturgical takbīr.\n- Root: صلا (ṣ-l-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Root denotes supplication (duʿā'), blessing, and the ritual prayer; al-ṣalāh as worship with bowing and prostration.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-ṣalāh is fundamentally supplication and seeking forgiveness; in the Law it is the specific acts of worship comprising standing, bowing, and prostration, with the heart present in humility.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: the prescribed prayer (al-ṣalāh al-maktūbah). Metaphorical: \"ṣallā ʿalā\" for invoking blessings (on the Prophet), and \"muṣallīn\" for those who pray or supplicate.\n- Root: سجد (s-j-d)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Prostration; placing the forehead on the ground in worship.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Al-sujūd is fundamentally humility and self-abasement; it is made a term for humbling oneself before Allah in worship — two kinds: voluntary (for humans, deserving reward) and compelled/subjugated (for all creation).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: prostration in prayer. Metaphorical: \"sajadat al-safīnah lil-riyāḥ\" (the ship yields to the winds), and \"ʿayn sājidah\" (a languid eye) — indicating submission or stillness.\n- Sibawayh Rule: Rule of Restriction and Focused Predication (al-ḥaṣr wa al-taqyīd bi-innamā) — Used in the text's argumentation (e.g., \"إنما أوردناها في هذا القسم لأنها تتكرر\") to restrict the reason for inclusion, and in preference statements (\"والمختار أن الجماعة أفضل\") to assert a focused judgment.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 400, 2663], [2, 2663, 4605], [3, 4605, 5329], [4, 5329, 6575], [5, 6575, 7952]], "2": [[1, 350, 1675], [2, 1675, 3038], [3, 3038, 3555], [4, 3555, 4411], [5, 4411, 5357]], "3": [[1, 350, 1266], [2, 1266, 2278], [3, 2278, 3045], [4, 3045, 3780], [5, 3780, 4462], [6, 4462, 5122]], "4": [[1, 400, 1534], [2, 1534, 3443], [3, 3443, 5149], [4, 5149, 6342], [5, 6342, 7368], [6, 7368, 8478], [7, 8478, 9301], [8, 9301, 9957], [9, 9957, 10721]], "5": [[1, 350, 1048], [2, 1048, 1501], [3, 1501, 2491], [4, 2491, 3401], [5, 3401, 4260]]}, "minshawi": {"1": [[1, 200, 3602], [2, 3602, 5643], [3, 5643, 6412], [4, 6412, 7714], [5, 7714, 9150]], "2": [[1, 350, 2637], [2, 2637, 4105], [3, 4105, 4841], [4, 4841, 5716], [5, 5716, 6680]], "3": [[1, 200, 1457], [2, 1457, 2843], [3, 2843, 3915], [4, 3915, 4829], [5, 4829, 5743], [6, 5743, 6630]], "4": [[1, 200, 1461], [2, 1461, 4101], [3, 4101, 6489], [4, 6489, 8347], [5, 8347, 9488], [6, 9488, 10722], [7, 10722, 11571], [8, 11571, 12301], [9, 12301, 13150]], "5": [[1, 380, 1389], [2, 1389, 2036], [3, 2036, 3518], [4, 3518, 4779], [5, 4779, 5980]]}, "abdulbasit_warsh": {"97:1": [[1, 600, 2097], [2, 2097, 4343], [3, 4343, 4772], [4, 4772, 5844], [5, 5844, 8915]], "1": [[1, 600, 2097], [2, 2097, 4343], [3, 4343, 4772], [4, 4772, 5844], [5, 5844, 8915]], "97:2": [[1, 593, 1575], [2, 1575, 3173], [3, 3173, 3603], [4, 3603, 4366], [5, 4366, 6590]], "2": [[1, 593, 1575], [2, 1575, 3173], [3, 3173, 3603], [4, 3603, 4366], [5, 4366, 6590]], "97:3": [[1, 530, 1322], [2, 1322, 2504], [3, 2504, 3239], [4, 3239, 3741], [5, 3741, 4404], [6, 4404, 5885]], "3": [[1, 530, 1322], [2, 1322, 2504], [3, 2504, 3239], [4, 3239, 3741], [5, 3741, 4404], [6, 4404, 5885]], "97:4": [[1, 600, 1777], [2, 1777, 4665], [3, 4665, 6655], [4, 6655, 7707], [5, 7707, 8937], [6, 8937, 10028], [7, 10028, 10584], [8, 10584, 11204], [9, 11204, 13513]], "4": [[1, 600, 1777], [2, 1777, 4665], [3, 4665, 6655], [4, 6655, 7707], [5, 7707, 8937], [6, 8937, 10028], [7, 10028, 10584], [8, 10584, 11204], [9, 11204, 13513]], "97:5": [[1, 473, 1226], [2, 1226, 1640], [3, 1640, 2473], [4, 2473, 3221], [5, 3221, 5258]], "5": [[1, 473, 1226], [2, 1226, 1640], [3, 1640, 2473], [4, 2473, 3221], [5, 3221, 5258]]}}, "letterTiming": {"abdulbasit": {"97:1": [{"wordIdx": 0, "charIdx": 0, "char": "إ", "grapheme": "إِ", "start": 400, "end": 748, "duration": 348, "peakTime": 574}, {"wordIdx": 0,